			<article>
				<p class="eyebrow">How-to guide</p>
				<h1>Install Anywhere</h1>
				<p class="lede">Install the desktop app on macOS, Linux, or Windows, then install the <code>anywhere</code> command line tool if you want to start sessions from scripts and other agents.</p>
				<p>Anywhere is free and MIT licensed. Every download is on the <a href="https://github.com/mingo023/anywhere/releases">GitHub releases page</a>.</p>

				<h2 id="install-on-macos">Install on macOS</h2>
				<p>Anywhere needs macOS 13 or later. The app is a universal binary for Apple silicon and Intel Macs, signed and notarized.</p>
				<ol>
					<li>Download <a href="https://github.com/mingo023/anywhere/releases/latest/download/Anywhere.dmg">Anywhere.dmg</a>.</li>
					<li>Open the file and drag <strong>Anywhere</strong> to <strong>Applications</strong>.</li>
					<li>Open Anywhere.</li>
				</ol>
				<p>On first launch, the app registers its background service, pocketd, as a login item. If you turn it off in the macOS Login Items settings, Anywhere says <strong>Anywhere's background service is off.</strong> and offers <strong>Open Login Items</strong>.</p>
				<p>Updates install through Sparkle. To check for one, open Settings with <kbd>⌘,</kbd>, select <strong>General</strong>, and click <strong>Check now</strong> under <strong>Software update</strong>. When an update is ready, click <strong>Restart to update</strong>. Agents and terminals keep running through an update.</p>

				<h2 id="install-on-linux-or-windows">Install on Linux or Windows</h2>
				<p>Anywhere publishes a build for Linux on x86_64. It is unsigned and has no updater. To update, download the new archive.</p>
				<p>The latest release doesn't include a Windows desktop archive. Check the <a href="https://github.com/mingo023/anywhere/releases">releases page</a> for a newer one. Windows machines can still be <a href="/docs/hosts">hosts</a>.</p>
				<ol>
					<li>Download the archive for your system:
						<ul>
							<li>Linux: <a href="https://github.com/mingo023/anywhere/releases/latest/download/Anywhere-linux-amd64.tar.gz">Anywhere-linux-amd64.tar.gz</a></li>
						</ul>
					</li>
					<li>Unpack it. You get an <code>Anywhere</code> folder that holds <code>pocket-desktop</code> and <code>pocketd</code>.</li>
					<li>Run <code>pocket-desktop</code> from that folder. On Windows, run <code>pocket-desktop.exe</code>.</li>
				</ol>
				<p>On first launch, pocketd installs itself as a background service. On Linux it is a systemd user service. On Windows it is a scheduled task.</p>

				<h2 id="install-an-agent">Install an agent</h2>
				<p>Anywhere doesn't include any agent. It runs the agent command line tools it finds on your login <code>PATH</code>. Install at least one and sign in to it. The commands for each agent are in <a href="/docs/agents">Supported agents</a>.</p>
				<p>If you install an agent while Anywhere is open, restart Anywhere so it finds the agent.</p>

				<h2 id="install-the-anywhere-command">Install the anywhere command</h2>
				<p>The <code>anywhere</code> command starts sessions, sends prompts, reads replies, and edits Board tickets from a shell. It is pocketd run under the name <code>anywhere</code>. Installing it also installs a skill that tells Claude Code and Codex how to use it.</p>

				<h3>On macOS</h3>
				<ol>
					<li>Open Settings with <kbd>⌘,</kbd> and select <strong>General</strong>.</li>
					<li>Under <strong>Startup &amp; background</strong>, find <strong>Command line tool</strong> and click <strong>Install</strong>.</li>
					<li>Enter your Mac password when macOS asks for it.</li>
				</ol>
				<p>The row now says <strong>anywhere is on your PATH</strong>. Anywhere linked <code>/usr/local/bin/anywhere</code> to the pocketd inside the app and ran <code>pocketd skill install</code>.</p>
				<div class="callout">
					<p><span class="callout-title">Note</span>The <strong>Install</strong> button is only in release builds on macOS. Other builds show <strong>Comes with release builds on macOS</strong>.</p>
				</div>

				<h3>On Linux</h3>
				<ol>
					<li>Make a link named <code>anywhere</code> in a folder on your <code>PATH</code> that points at <code>pocketd</code> in the unpacked <code>Anywhere</code> folder. For example, from the folder that holds <code>Anywhere</code>:
				<pre><code>ln -s "$PWD/Anywhere/pocketd" ~/.local/bin/anywhere</code></pre>
					</li>
					<li>Install the skill:
				<pre><code>Anywhere/pocketd skill install</code></pre>
					</li>
				</ol>

				<h3>Check the command</h3>
				<p>Open a new terminal outside Anywhere and list your projects:</p>
				<pre><code>anywhere project list</code></pre>
				<p>The command prints each project's name and path. For every subcommand, see <a href="/docs/cli">The anywhere command</a>.</p>

				<h2 id="choose-what-closing-the-window-does">Choose what closing the window does</h2>
				<p>On macOS, closing the window leaves Anywhere running in the background by default, so the Dock badge and notifications stay. Agents keep running either way, because pocketd runs them.</p>
				<ol>
					<li>Open Settings with <kbd>⌘,</kbd> and select <strong>General</strong>.</li>
					<li>Under <strong>Quitting &amp; sleep</strong>, set <strong>When the window closes</strong> to <strong>Stay in the background</strong> or <strong>Quit Anywhere</strong>.</li>
				</ol>
				<p>To open Anywhere when you log in, turn on <strong>Open at login</strong> under <strong>Startup &amp; background</strong>.</p>
